Manager, I found the issue. Your `firebase.json` file only has Firestore rules configuration—it's missing the hosting configuration entirely. That's why the deployment only pushed the database rules and not your actual website files.

Here's what your current `firebase.json` contains:
```json
{
  "firestore": {
    "rules": "firestore.rules"
  }
}
```

You need to add a hosting section. Update `firebase.json` to:

```json
{
  "firestore": {
    "rules": "firestore.rules"
  },
  "hosting": {
    "public": "dist",
    "ignore": [
      "firebase.json",
      "**/.*",
      "**/node_modules/**"
    ],
    "rewrites": [
      {
        "source": "**",
        "destination": "/index.html"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

Then deploy again:

```bash
npm run build
firebase deploy --only hosting
```

The key addition is `"public": "dist"` which tells Firebase to upload your built Vite output (the `dist/` folder created by `npm run build`). After this deployment, your app will be live at `https://manhattan-cafe-9fe21.web.app`.

